> # ================================================================
> # Task 44 - Figures for report.md (tasks of 2026-09-28)
> # Date: Sep 29, 2026
> #
> # One figure for each finding that report.md showed only as a table.
> # The RRBS figures (items 4, 5 and 6) read the Task 39 and Task 41
> # outputs, and Fig21 also reads the RRBS data. Items 1 and 3 read
> # the Task 40 and Task 36 outputs. Nothing is re-estimated here:
> # every number drawn comes from the file named in the caption.
> #
> #   Fig20  item 4(1)  RRBS: missing data, and IQR outliers
> #   Fig21  item 6     RRBS: the six states, one real site each
> #   Fig22  item 4(2)  RRBS: nearby sites share a state
> #   Fig23  item 5     RRBS: agreement vs correlation, by state pair
> #   Fig24  item 5     RRBS: scores by distance, true neighbours
> #   Fig25  item 5     RRBS: real pairs vs patient-shuffled pairs
> #   Fig26  item 1(3)  what the +100 offset does to beta
> #   Fig27  item 3     OutlierMeth with the CG ID replaced or removed
> #   Fig28  item 1(1)  probes that map to more than one place
> #   Fig29  item 2     L-state red dots and the most flagged samples
> #                     (also writes Task44_Item2_LRedDotsByFlagRank.csv)
> #
> # STYLE
> #   Reference palette of the dataviz method, light surface #fcfcfb:
> #   series blue #2a78d6, orange #eb6834, aqua #1baf7a (checked with
> #   validate_palette.js, all pairs; aqua is below 3:1 contrast, so it
> #   is always labelled directly). Status colours appear only in Fig27,
> #   where a cell means works / fails, and always with a text label.
> #   Solid hairline grid, 2px lines, dots with a surface ring.
> #
> # PRIVACY
> #   No figure names a sample or ties a sample to a site. Fig21 shows
> #   the 18 values of six unnamed sites, one per state.
> # ================================================================
> 
